      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Rationalizing gives \\[ \\frac1{x+\\sqrt{x^2+1}}=\\sqrt{x^2+1}-x. \\] The entire expression is therefore \\(2x.\\) It is rational exactly when \\(x\\) is rational.\n\nThus the correct answer is B.",
